her  information including the news and at  the same time to connect to people so  it's really our main source of  information here in the Philippines  Filipinos spend more than four hours a  day on social media with Facebook being  the most popular platform with nearly 84  million users in 2022  a survey here recently showed that more  than half of the people who said that  they're using social media as their news  source find it very difficult to  distinguish between what's true and  what's false on social media so uh you  can just imagine the extent of that  problem  the 2018 Cambridge analytica Scandal saw  the data mining firm questioned over its  work for Donald Trump's presidential  campaign  one whistleblower described how  questionable rule of law high social  media usage and corrupt politicians made  the Philippines the perfect place to  test the limits of online manipulation  at some point we were called patient  zero when it comes to this information  brexit the election that Trump won these  are also events that showcased how much  social media use can shape public  opinion but this time around it's really  supercharged  there's a feeling that it's been well  structured institutionalized it really  shows that you can win an election based  on an image you have built on social  media  bongbong Marcos has been building his  online presence for over a decade during  his unsuccessful 2016 run for vice  president he relied heavily on online  messaging  these 2022 campaign he sized up  traditional media instead speaking  directly to voters online in short video  blogs he gets a lot of engagements for  that and a lot of people like that about  him the Vlog thing they really patronize  that because I guess it humanizes him  I've seen analysis on social media  saying that he intentionally did not  attend debates and interviews because  that was what contributed to his loss in  2016 so there was a revisiting of the  strategy the campaign strategy and as we  are able to see now we could say that it  has been effective  Facebooks and YouTube's Instagram  Twitter  bongbong has over 7 million followers on  Facebook and another 2 million on  YouTube his supporters flood news feeds  and message boards with election  messages  [Music]  but political posts and videos are often  disguised  a lot of the disinformation that  spreading on social media especially in  the lead up to the elections come in the  form of news some are quoting  personalities  inaccurately but are presented in such a  way that they look like and even imitate  the colors of mainstream media we found  out that out of the 300 plus fact checks  that we produced for online  disinformation  120 of them has something to do with  election related disinformation and a  huge number of that actually benefited  Marcos in a way that it hyped up his  presidential campaign and it also tried  to distort historical facts regarding  his family  [Music]  in the 1970s Ferdinand Marcos had led a  military government of uncommon  brutality  he disbanded Congress silenced the media  and used the Army to torture and kill  thousands of citizens  through all of this Marcos and his wife  Imelda became exceedingly Wealthy by  siphoning money from State funds  all the while the Philippines economy  crashed and many people suffered  [Music]  a critical part of bongbong marcos's  election campaign was convincing  millions of people these things simply  didn't happen  foreign  the pure hate that has been heaped upon  him over the last 30 plus years  his memory his legacy continues to  endure  it was portrayed by their supporters as  a period of prosperity despite economic  downturn that time and then it was also  portrayed that only enemies of the state  were killed extravagant parties on the  presidential yacht and then also um  there was a widespread denial about the  ill-gotten wealth Ferdinand Jr is the  man in the flashing bow tie and this  circulated mostly in social media and  that Legacy was the one that Ferdinand  Marcos Jr in their own words they tried  to present their version of that history  and that's what people are gonna believe  the love for the Marcus has never really  left here in the Philippines even after  they were ousted they maintained uh  quite a strong Bailey week in the  northern Philippines and that's where  the most loyal supporters are so this  effort to explain their side of History  became even more evident because of  social media that even went into  overdrive because of the pandemic when  people were stuck at home  social media when I talk to people and  ask them who they were inclined to  support if they said bongbong Marcos I  would say why and there would be this  Gauzy look in these sentiments expressed  like you know his father was a great man  he was a strong leader Philippines need  strong leadership now  and you would say okay well what about  this what about that what about the  other thing and they would blow it off  the response would tend to be one of two  things they would say oh look I was a  kid then or I wasn't born then it's  nothing to me  or they say it's fake news  tonight a brutal dictator's son winning  the presidential election in the  Philippines by a landslide  Marcos has been elected as the next  president of the Philippines and I think  that's a very telling indication as to  how successful this this information  campaign benefiting him is God bless the  Philippines God bless our work  the days after the election friends and  colleagues asked me  how could this happen  then I began to wonder whether the more  pertinent question was what was actually  going to stop it  it's hard to overstate how much online  disinformation propelled the success of  bongbong's campaign  but directly connecting social media  lies to their sources let alone anyone  directing the effort remains difficult  you have supporters real people and then  on the other hand you have fake accounts  and these fake accounts plus the real  people who are spreading this that  creates an ecosystem wherein this  information spreads  we're able to Monitor and flag these  online disinformation content but we  really cannot pinpoint who is the person  or the person but one thing I could tell  you is President bongbong Marcos he  likes to disassociate himself and his  team from this information campaign that  largely benefited him in fact he even  said that he's actually the victim of  fake news some people say that history  was revised online what do you what is  your response to that show me  show me where this revisionism well now  are part from our side whatever you want  to show me  uh anything that we have said we can  prove  the success of boom booms campaign can't  solely be attributed to social media  another major factor was the effect of  his running mate Sarah duterte daughter  of the previous president Rodrigo  duterte who remains popular in parts of  the Philippines this time around with  Sarah duterte running by his side he was  able to win those provinces in the  southern part of the country where the  duterte's hail from and he was able to  double the number of provinces that he  was able to win compared to his 2016  vice presidential race which he lost  it's really a consolidation of two  powerful political dynasties political  families one healing from the north  that's Marcos and the other hailing from  the south and that's duterte  the Philippines excels at dynastic  Politics the two presidents prior to  leader Rodrigo duterte they were  children of presidents  the lower House of our Congress we have  a majority and most of our lawmakers are  products of political dynasties there's  even a belief that the good traits the  leadership qualities of a father or a  parent is passed down to his or her  child so that's how much political  dynasties are welcomed and elected here  in the Philippines  while Marcos and duterte ran on a ticket  of national Unity online their  supporters pushed lies and attacked the  opposition candidate Lenny robredo  you would tend to say that we shouldn't  focus on the negative things and instead  focus on unity and nation building so  that's the official line but on Facebook  on social media you can see how much  vitriol there was especially against his  main opponent vice president Lenny  robredo Roberto has been called so many  names she was even accused of having an  affair her daughters were accused of  having sex scandals a lot of these  Facebook pages and Facebook groups that  were able to flag spreading this  information and misinformation some of  them carry his name in their account  names  um and we actually also observed and  back in 2021 that a lot of YouTube  videos that are misinforming people what  happens is um the video is uploaded on  YouTube and then there are a number of  Facebook pages that re-uploads it on  Facebook that also re-uploaded on tiktok  and this suggests that there is  automation or that only one person  administers or moderates these accounts  and so it also suggests that there is a  an organized effort or campaign with  regards to  um spreading Miss and disinformation  my father built more and better roads  produced more rice than all  administrations before his  so will it be with his son you will get  no excuses from me  now as president bongbong Marcos bashens  himself as a pragmatist focused on  quality of life issues  on foreign policy he's promised to grow  closer relations with China even as the  two countries Clash over fishing rights  in the South China Sea  all the while maintaining historic links  to the USA  this idea or this feeling or this  shall we say opinion I have of my father  of the man  has just been strengthened as time goes  on what's also noteworthy is bongbong  never talked about marcelona in a  negative light it's all about admiration  for his father a promise to continue the  good projects that came out of that era  it's really an indication that you can  win an election based on a particular  image that you shaped on social media  for some there is frustration that lies  have won over facts but there's also  concern that things will only get worse  over the course of this six-year  presidential term the facts of the past  is not really as effective as the facts  of the present and the future maybe it's  because the people now cannot relate  with whatever happened during the  martial law of Marco senior and they  actually only care about what's going to  happen to them now and what's going to  happen in the future and Marcus Jr  apparently was able to present himself  effectively as someone who will bring  about positive change who will bring  hope and who will unify the country  towards a better tomorrow or a better  future  if you're gonna get a platform like  social media that reaches a lot of  people you're gonna create a way by  which this version of history is going  to spread and your supporters are gonna  spread and believe it  Imelda Marcos famously said in one of  the documentaries about her perception  is real and the truth is not  our job as fact Checkers and not only  fact Checkers but as journalists as  amplifiers of truth would be more  challenging in the next  um six years because we see the election  of a president whose campaign was based  on this information and lies so we have  to be ready for the challenges that this  Administration would entail so yeah  um we're we're preparing for it and  hopefully we could go through it  um without any problem  foreign  [Music]  [Music]

